WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.990
I don't know if you guys remember, but about
a year ago, there was a movement that called

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:13.299
itself, I guess, classical liberalism, which
claimed to be part of some new center of American

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:14.299
politics.

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:18.660
And in reality, it was a complete and total
ruse.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:25.000
What they wanted to do was to sort of normalize
whacky libertarian conservatism as if it were

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.890
the new center of American politics when it
really wasn't the new center of American politics.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.989
But just because that movement was wrong in
identifying a new center doesn't mean that

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:39.100
there isn't an identifiable new center.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.660
And that's what I want to talk about today.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.129
And I think the context that will be relevant
and interesting here is that if we on the

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:53.350
left want to keep moving ourselves to the
left as a country, we want to understand the

00:00:53.350 --> 00:01:01.050
areas in which the average of the country
would be liable to side with us rather than

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.949
to be pulled further to the right.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:07.790
Now, I don't know if this is necessary, but
as a quick disclaimer, before we jump into

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.460
this, this new center that I'm going to describe
to you.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.170
These are not my views.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.630
I need to I know that if I don't do this,
I will have 100 messages tomorrow from people

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.340
saying, David, you centrist shill.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.090
It is I know we're not used to it with Donald
Trump, who's in who's unable to do any kind

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.760
of abstract thinking.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.670
But I'm going to describe to you a set of
beliefs that is not mine.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.020
So these are not my beliefs.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.630
I'm to the left of this new center.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.399
Now, that being said, let's get into the details.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:42.710
Gallup did a very interesting study, which
they've done for 20 to 40 years on different

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:43.960
issues.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.450
And they looked at where is the country right
now on a variety of different issues.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:54.299
And they've represented the issues as well
as the shift in opinion visually.

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:56.790
And we're putting that up on the screen for
our visual audience.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.630
But I'm also going to describe it to you.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:05.110
And this lets us build up a sort of picture
of where the middle is right now in America.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.110
On a number of issues.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.969
So let's go through the eight issues.

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:08.969
So on.

00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:16.820
On gun sales, the center, the average of the
country right now, the middle wants more strict

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.060
gun sales laws than those that we've had in
the past.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:26.200
The center believes that religion is fairly
important, but not very important.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.300
The center thinks that military spending is
about right, believes the earth should be

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:37.560
prioritized over the economy and that immigration
law should more or less stay the same in terms

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.700
of the number of immigrants coming into the
United States.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.680
The center, as of today, thinks that the federal
income tax is just about right.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.621
They don't think it should be raised, but
they don't think it should be lowered, that

00:02:48.621 --> 00:02:54.340
abortion should be legal sometimes, but not
always, and that marijuana should be legalized.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.290
So remember, this is just an average of the
middle.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:04.190
But what's extremely interesting about this
is that it proves that the new center is not

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.600
libertarian.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.100
It is not classically liberal.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.290
And you really need to look at the details
to understand this new center as an example.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:19.930
If the new center were merely libertarian,
it wouldn't favor stricter gun laws, for example.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.580
It wouldn't favor prioritizing the earth over
the economy because that is code for.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.200
We've got to regulate business activity.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:33.520
If the center were libertarian, it wouldn't
think immigration laws were just about right.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.340
Because true libertarians want total mobility
of labor, and that's not what we currently

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:39.340
have.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:45.530
What's also important to understand about
how we came to this new center is how opinion

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.980
on these eight issues has shifted over time.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:54.400
So, again, looking at one example, in the
early 90s, much of the gun laws should be

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.150
made more strict.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.820
That changed until 2010, when people wanted
looser and looser gun laws.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:06.220
And then since 2010, we've seen a reversal
which has very strongly returned to the early

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.100
90s numbers where the center wants stricter
gun laws.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.470
So does the left as well.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.910
Religion has been much more steady and it's
change over time.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.630
The center of America has found religion less
and less important over time, where it now

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.790
finds it fairly but not very important.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:31.200
Military spending has moved pretty radically,
often in concert with what's going on militarily

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.200
at the time.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.760
And then, interestingly, if you look at the
trends on immigration, it is very steady over

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:43.910
the last 40 years that immigration to the
United States should show, generally speaking,

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.550
be increased.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:51.390
Ending up sort of that it's okay where it
is and then probably not surprisingly, on

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.000
marijuana.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.960
It's been a steady increase in the proportion
of Americans that believe cannabis should

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.960
be.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:04:59.960
Legalized.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:02.090
So why do we care about this again?

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:07.020
If we want to build the left, we must understand
where the center is.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.200
If we misunderstand where the center is, we
are not going to properly structure our platform.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.040
The center is not some small government, pro-business,
conservative.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:25.420
The way we would sometimes be be convinced
Mitt Romney is not the center.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.370
Mitt Romney is far more reasonable than Donald
Trump.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.030
Mitt Romney is far less offensive and dangerous
than Donald Trump.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.220
But Mitt Romney is not the center.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.150
And that's important to understand.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:38.890
When the left thinks the center is something
that it's not.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.910
It tries to appeal to the center in the wrong
ways.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.470
So let me know what you think.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:48.760
I think that this new center represents a
lot of the changes we've been following in

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:56.170
the United States, which would include a sort
of status quo perspective on some issues and

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.180
a progressive ization on other issues.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.180
Let me know what you think.

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.540
Let me know, importantly, how you think our
understanding of this new center could be

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:09.880
used to bring more people, tourists to our
side and to really push progressive change

